From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kirk <hello@kirkdiamond.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: draw the right iMac 5K tile's cursor on DCE

On the merged 5K output the right tile's hardware cursor is programmed
by amdgpu_dm_imac5k_update_companion_cursor() at the cursor's screen
position minus the tile origin (half the mode width). That is right on
DCN, which takes screen positions. DCE places the cursor at a position
in the framebuffer instead ("avivo cursor are offset into the total
surface", dce_v10_0.c; dce110_set_cursor_position() only adds the
plane's source offset). The right tile shows the framebuffer from the
tile origin on, so on the iMac Pro (DCE 12) its cursor landed in the
left half of the framebuffer and was never drawn: the pointer vanished
as it crossed the seam, while hover and clicks still worked.

On DCE, add the tile origin back to the right tile's cursor position.
A cursor straddling the seam keeps its hotspot shift, so its right part
is drawn from the tile's left edge. DCN (iMac20,x) is unchanged.

Found on an iMac Pro (iMacPro1,1) running the merged output:
the cursor disappeared on the right half of the panel.

Written with an AI coding assistant (Claude Code, Claude Opus 5.5) from
that hardware report; tested on an iMac Pro (iMacPro1,1, Fedora 45):
the pointer shows on both halves and across the seam.

Signed-off-by: Kirk <hello@kirkdiamond.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c	2026-11-20 14:44:24.909792001 +0000
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c	2026-11-20 14:44:38.628792008 +0000
@@ -4252,6 +4252,16 @@
 	if (amdgpu_dm_plane_get_cursor_position(plane, comp, &position))
 		return;
 
+	/*
+	 * DCE places the cursor at a position in the framebuffer, not on the
+	 * screen (see dce110_set_cursor_position()), and the right tile shows
+	 * the framebuffer from the tile origin on. Move the cursor back there,
+	 * or it lands in the left half and is never drawn. DCN takes screen
+	 * positions.
+	 */
+	if (position.enable && dm->dc->ctx->dce_version < DCE_VERSION_MAX)
+		position.x += amdgpu_dm_imac5k_tile_origin(comp, plane->state->state);
+
 	if (!position.enable) {
 		if (!comp_state->stream->cursor_position.enable)
 			return;
-- 
